## Why This Is Asked
Tests dynamic cross-DC routing control and zero-downtime config updates in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts
- etcd as central config store
- sidecar watching and config generation
- nginx config fragmenting and graceful reload
- cross-DC raft replication
- observability via Prometheus

## Code Example

```yaml
# example fragment regenerated by sidecar
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  server_name tenant.example.com;
  location / {
    proxy_pass http://api-primary:8080;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle watch failures or conflicts?
- How to scale the sidecar to many tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical ability to extend a docker-dca setup with a compliant, low-latency data-redaction path.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config-driven per-tenant policies
- Sidecar pattern and in-memory caching
- Streaming JSON redaction without full buffering
- Nginx-edge integration and TLS context

## Code Example
```go
package main
import (
  "encoding/json"
  "fmt"
)
func redact(m map[string]interface{}, fields map[string]bool){
  for k,v := range m {
    if fields[k] { m[k] = "***REDACTED***"; continue }
    if mm, ok := v.(map[string]interface{}); ok { redact(mm, fields) }
    if arr, ok := v.([]interface{}); ok {
      for _, it := range arr { if sub, ok := it.(map[string]interface{}); ok { redact(sub, fields) } }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test nested JSON redaction with large bodies?
- How would you monitor redaction performance without affecting latency?
